Consumer merge plus diff plus queue plus cancellation plus aggregate stay
qualified with fixture evidence (issue #509).

Merge validates the proposed merge, not the contributor branch alone.
Validate the proposed merge with the same test-merge snapshot.
All selected checks in a run use the same test-merge snapshot with its
PR-head and target-branch revisions recorded. Map findings back to valid
PR-diff source locations. If conflicts prevent test-merge creation,
report validation as blocked without head-only fallback or aggregate
success. The blocked-status path is qualified without executing fork
code with reporting privileges.

Diff placement never narrows scope: documentation-only and mixed changes
still invoke all selected checks at normal scope, and diff-based review
placement does not narrow analysis scope. Unmappable findings stay in
reports and summary counts, never on invented lines, with no invented
review locations.

Queue is consumer-native: consumers enable and configure their queue.
Queue checks use the same selected checks and stable aggregate identity,
bound to the queue revision rather than an individual PR head. Queue runs
never create, update, or clean up PR comments/threads. Obsolete queue
results cannot satisfy a newer queue revision. Queue membership does not
grant fork code secrets or write credentials.

Cancellation is concurrency-scoped: group
dx-ci-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.event.pull_request.number ||
github.ref }} with cancel-in-progress true. New PR commits automatically
cancel superseded integration runs for that PR in either scheduling mode.
Scope PR supersession to that PR's integration runs, not other PRs or
queue runs. Retain prior run history under normal retention; unfinished
or cancelled checks are not passed. Late callbacks must not overwrite
current summaries or modify current threads, even when cancellation races
completion.

Aggregate is the single stable dx-ci check: needs platforms-gate, lint,
typecheck, format, generate, security-audit, license-audit, test, build,
coverage with if always(). Disabled checks report skipped and stay green;
every other non-success names its failing checks and fails the aggregate
so the stable required check never hides a failing selection. Missing,
blocked, unexpectedly skipped, cancelled, or incomplete selected results
cannot produce success. Consumers require the aggregate in branch
protection with latest-target validation; the integration never modifies
those settings itself.

Seed only for platform plus consumer plus release evidence; no
Supported claim. Live merge-queue runs plus required-check bindings
beyond static wiring stay owned under issue #509 tracker with native
GitHub semantics.
